om2
note tools/flow.om: the decision core of the Omega merge queue for one Radicle repository, in pure
note seeded Omega.
note
note A repository's open patches wait for the default branch. For one default-branch head this
note program decides what each patch needs next and writes the plan as the POSIX sh script that
note carries it out, so every decision is made from data, never by hand. Build with the seed-born
note compiler:
note   omc < tools/flow.om > flow && chmod +x flow
note   { printf 'target x86linux\n'; cat tools/flow.om; } | omc-x86 > flow   (native x86-64)
note Run:
note   flow BRANCH GATE STATE RECEIPTS OUT
note   BRANCH    exactly 40 lowercase hex digits: the default-branch head the plan is for
note   GATE      exactly 40 lowercase hex digits: the git blob id of build.sh at BRANCH
note   STATE     read: the open patches. The header line is exactly
note               patch TAB head TAB tree TAB rel
note             then one patch per line, exactly 4 TAB-separated fields:
note               patch    40 lowercase hex digits, the patch id
note               head     40 lowercase hex digits, the patch head commit
note               tree     40 lowercase hex digits, the tree of that commit
note               rel      ff (BRANCH is an ancestor of head), div (the two diverged) or in
note                        (head is already in BRANCH)
note             A patch id appears once. The header alone is valid. At most 4096 rows and 4 MiB.
note   RECEIPTS  read: the receipt ledger. The header line is exactly
note               tree TAB gate TAB verdict TAB log
note             then one receipt per line, exactly 4 TAB-separated fields:
note               tree     40 lowercase hex digits, the tree that was gated
note               gate     40 lowercase hex digits, the blob of the build.sh that gated it
note               verdict  pass or fail
note               log      64 lowercase hex digits, the sha256 of the gate's log
note             A (tree, gate) pair appears once, even with the same verdict. At most 16384 rows
note             and 4 MiB. Only rows whose gate is GATE are consulted.
note             In both files every line ends in a newline: an empty file, a blank line, a CR
note             anywhere or a last line without its newline is refused.
note   OUT       written: the script.
note Decision for each STATE row, in input order, with r the receipt for (the row's tree, GATE):
note   1. rel in                                        merged  (whatever r says)
note   2. r pass, rel ff, no earlier row got merge      merge
note      r pass, rel ff, an earlier row got merge      queued  (one merge per plan; the next
note                                                             plan, made after it, decides)
note      r pass, rel div                               rebase
note   3. r fail                                        fail
note   4. no r, no earlier row has the same tree        gate
note      no r, an earlier row has the same tree        same    (a tree is gated once)
note   In rule 4 every earlier row with that tree counts, whatever its own decision; with no
note   receipt for the tree they all lack one.
note Lookups go through open-addressing hash tables (FNV-1a 64 over the hex bytes, linear probing,
note never more than half full): receipts by (tree, gate), patches by id, trees seen so far by
note tree. The same tables find the duplicates, so a run is linear in the input size.
note The script: a fixed comment header; "# plan-branch BRANCH", "# plan-gate GATE" and
note "# plan-counts patches N merged A merge B queued C rebase D fail E gate F same G" (N rows,
note then the rows given each decision); a blank line; branch='BRANCH' and gate='GATE'; the fixed
note shell body, which checks the repository against BRANCH and GATE and defines fl_die, fl_git,
note fl_tree, fl_gate and fl_merge; then for every row, in input order,
note "# plan ACTION PATCH HEAD TREE", followed for merge by "fl_merge 'PATCH' 'HEAD' 'TREE'" and
note for gate by "fl_gate 'PATCH' 'HEAD' 'TREE'"; last "echo 'flow: step done'". Every value in
note the script is validated hex, so none needs quoting beyond its single quotes.
note Exit 0 when OUT is written; 2 for the wrong number of arguments, with the usage line on
note stderr; 1 for any refusal, with one stderr line "flow: ..." that names the argument, or the
note file and its line, and OUT not opened (the script is built in memory and written once, at
note the end). The output depends only on the arguments and the input bytes: no clock, no
note environment.

note the input regions of inp: STATE at 0, RECEIPTS at RB (each 4 MiB and one byte to see the
note end), BRANCH at BO and GATE at GO (40 bytes each). Every byte compared or copied lives here.
const RB ulong 4194312
const BO ulong 8388624
const GO ulong 8388664
global inp uchar 8388704
note the script bytes
global ob uchar 4194304
global obn ulong 1
note the path named by the current argument
global pb uchar 4096
global pbn ulong 1
note STATE rows: line offset, rel (1 ff, 2 div, 3 in), decision; and the row count
global so ulong 4096
global sr ulong 4096
global sa ulong 4096
global ns ulong 1
note RECEIPTS rows: line offset, verdict (1 pass, 2 fail)
global ro ulong 16384
global rv ulong 16384
note hash tables, each slot row index + 1 or 0 for empty: receipts by tree and gate, patches by
note id, trees seen by tree
global hr ulong 32768
global hp ulong 8192
global ht ulong 8192
note the current line's 4 fields: offset and length of each
global fld ulong 8
note rows per decision: merged merge queued rebase fail gate same
global cnt ulong 7

text tpre "flow: "
text tnl "\n"
text tusage "usage: flow BRANCH GATE STATE RECEIPTS OUT\n"
text targ "cannot read a command-line argument"
text tbr "BRANCH is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text tgt "GATE is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text topen "cannot open "
text tread "cannot read "
text tbig "file over 4 MiB: "
text twrite "cannot write "
text toverf "script over the 4 MiB buffer"
text tline ": line "
text tcol ": "
text tempty "empty file"
text tnonl "no newline at the end of the line"
text tblank "blank line"
text tcr "carriage return in the line"
text tcols "row needs exactly 4 TAB-separated fields"
text tshdr "patch\thead\ttree\trel"
text trhdr "tree\tgate\tverdict\tlog"
text tbsh "header line is not patch TAB head TAB tree TAB rel"
text tbrh "header line is not tree TAB gate TAB verdict TAB log"
text tmanys "more than 4096 rows"
text tmanyr "more than 16384 rows"
text tbpa "patch is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text tbhd "head is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text tbtr "tree is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text tbrel "rel is not ff, div or in"
text tbgt "gate is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text tbvd "verdict is not pass or fail"
text tblog "log is not 64 lowercase hex digits"
text tdupp "patch already on line "
text tdupr "tree and gate already on line "
text rff "ff"
text rdiv "div"
text rin "in"
text vpass "pass"
text vfail "fail"
note the decision names, by code 0..6 (fail is vfail)
text n0 "merged"
text n1 "merge"
text n2 "queued"
text n3 "rebase"
text n5 "gate"
text n6 "same"
text pbr "# plan-branch "
text pgt "\n# plan-gate "
text pc0 "\n# plan-counts patches "
text pc1 " merged "
text pc2 " merge "
text pc3 " queued "
text pc4 " rebase "
text pc5 " fail "
text pc6 " gate "
text pc7 " same "
text pv1 "\n\nbranch='"
text pv2 "'\ngate='"
text q2 "' '"
text q3 "'\n"
text sp " "
text pln "# plan "
text fm "fl_merge '"
text fg "fl_gate '"
text tend "echo 'flow: step done'\n"

note the fixed parts of the script, paragraph by paragraph: the comment header (h0, h1), then the
note body (b0 checks, b1 fl_tree, b2 fl_gate, b3 fl_merge)
text h0 "#!/bin/sh\n# flow.sh: one step of the Omega merge queue for one Radicle repository.\n# Generated by tools/flow.om from the repository's open patches and its receipt ledger; do not\n# edit by hand.\n#\n# A patch merges only as a fast-forward of the default branch, and only when a receipt says the\n# default branch's gate passed on the patch head's exact tree, so the default branch only ever\n# moves to a tree that passed the gate guarding it. A patch whose tree has no receipt is gated:\n# the default branch's build.sh, never the patch's own, runs in a worktree of the patch head,\n# and the verdict goes into the ledger and onto the patch as a comment. A tree is gated once,\n# however many patches carry it, and never again while the gate is unchanged.\n#\n"
text h1 "#   sh flow.sh REPO DEFAULT RECEIPTS\n# REPO      a Radicle working copy, fetched, with its delegate's key authenticated (rad auth)\n# DEFAULT   the name of its default branch\n# RECEIPTS  the receipt ledger this plan was made from; new verdicts are appended to it\n# Exit status: 0 the step ran; 1 the repository is not as planned, or a gate, comment or push\n# could not run; 2 usage.\n# Each patch's decision is one \"# plan ACTION PATCH HEAD TREE\" line, in the order of the input.\n"
text b0 "set -eu\numask 022\n[ $# -eq 3 ] || { echo 'usage: sh flow.sh REPO DEFAULT RECEIPTS' >&2; exit 2; }\nrepo=$1 def=$2 rec=$3\nfl_die() { printf 'flow: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nfl_git() { git -C \"$repo\" \"$@\"; }\ncommand -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || fl_die \"git is required\"\ncommand -v rad >/dev/null 2>&1 || fl_die \"rad is required: https://radicle.xyz\"\n[ -f \"$rec\" ] || fl_die \"no receipt ledger $rec\"\ncur=$(fl_git rev-parse --verify -q \"refs/remotes/rad/$def^{commit}\") || fl_die \"$repo has no rad/$def\"\n[ \"$cur\" = \"$branch\" ] || fl_die \"rad/$def is $cur, not $branch: make a new plan\"\n[ \"$(fl_git rev-parse --verify -q \"$branch:build.sh\")\" = \"$gate\" ] || fl_die \"build.sh at $branch is not blob $gate\"\nfl_work=$(mktemp -d)\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$fl_work\"; fl_git worktree prune' EXIT\n"
text b1 "trap 'exit 1' HUP INT TERM\nfl_tree() { # fl_tree PATCH HEAD TREE: HEAD must be a commit whose tree is TREE\n  [ \"$(fl_git rev-parse --verify -q \"$2^{tree}\")\" = \"$3\" ] || fl_die \"patch $1: $2 is not a commit with tree $3\"\n}\n"
text b2 "fl_gate() { # fl_gate PATCH HEAD TREE: run the default branch's build.sh on HEAD; record and post the verdict\n  fl_tree \"$@\"\n  w=$fl_work/$3\n  fl_git worktree add -q --detach \"$w\" \"$2\" || fl_die \"patch $1: cannot check out $2\"\n  fl_git cat-file blob \"$gate\" > \"$w/build.sh\"\n  mkdir \"$w.home\"\n  # the gate never sees the delegate's key: no RAD_PASSPHRASE, RAD_SECRET, RAD_HOME, SSH_AUTH_SOCK or HOME\n  if (cd \"$w\" && env -u RAD_PASSPHRASE -u RAD_SECRET -u RAD_HOME -u SSH_AUTH_SOCK HOME=\"$w.home\" sh ./build.sh) > \"$w.log\" 2>&1; then v=pass; else v=fail; fi\n  l=$(sha256sum < \"$w.log\" | cut -c1-64)\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$3\" \"$gate\" \"$v\" \"$l\" >> \"$rec\"\n  m=\"flow gate $v tree $3 gate $gate log $l\"\n  f=$(sed -n '/^FAIL/{p;q;}' \"$w.log\")\n  [ -z \"$f\" ] || m=\"$m\n$f\"\n  (cd \"$repo\" && rad patch comment \"$1\" -m \"$m\" > /dev/null) || fl_die \"patch $1: cannot post the verdict\"\n  fl_git worktree remove --force \"$w\"\n  printf 'flow: gate %s patch %s tree %s\\n' \"$v\" \"$1\" \"$3\"\n}\n"
text b3 "fl_merge() { # fl_merge PATCH HEAD TREE: fast-forward DEFAULT to HEAD, whose tree passed the gate\n  fl_tree \"$@\"\n  fl_git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$branch\" \"$2\" || fl_die \"patch $1: $2 does not fast-forward $branch\"\n  fl_git push -q rad \"$2:refs/heads/$def\" || fl_die \"patch $1: the push of $2 to $def was refused\"\n  printf 'flow: merged patch %s head %s\\n' \"$1\" \"$2\"\n}\n\n"

note wdec: write v in decimal to stderr
fn wdec v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
k = ulong 20
note a ulong has at most 20 digits
while true bound 20
k = sub k 1
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
w = write 2 d k sub 20 k
end

note diem: refuse with m alone, then exit 1
fn diem m view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 m 0 len m
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note dief: refuse with m and the current path, then exit 1
fn dief m view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 m 0 len m
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note diel: refuse line ln of the current file with m, then the line number j when j is not 0;
note exit 1
fn diel m view uchar * ln ulong j ulong to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tline 0 len tline
wdec ln
w = write 2 tcol 0 len tcol
w = write 2 m 0 len m
if ne j 0
wdec j
end
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note chk: refuse line ln with m when ok is false
fn chk ok bool m view uchar * ln ulong to void
if not ok
diel m ln 0
end
end

note setpath: copy command-line argument ai into pb
fn setpath ai ulong to void
n = argread ai pb 0 4096
if le n 0
diem targ
end
put pbn 0 ulong n
end

note load: read the file named by argument ai into inp from b; return the offset of its end
fn load ai ulong b ulong to ulong
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
p = ulong 0
note every pass but the last reads at least one byte of the 4194305-byte region
while lt p 4194305 bound 4194306
k = read int fd inp add b p sub 4194305 p
if lt k 0
dief tread
end
if eq k 0
break
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if gt p 4194304
dief tbig
end
ret add b p
end

note wout: write ob to the file named by argument ai (created or truncated, mode 0644)
fn wout ai ulong to void
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 577 420
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
n = get obn 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 4194305
k = write int fd ob p sub n p
if le k 0
dief twrite
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ne c 0
dief twrite
end
end

note em: append a text to ob
fn em t view uchar * to void
p = get obn 0
n = len t
if gt n sub 4194304 p
diem toverf
end
for i ulong n bound 4194304
put ob add p i get t i
end
put obn 0 add p n
end

note emi: append n bytes of inp from o to ob
fn emi o ulong n ulong to void
p = get obn 0
if gt n sub 4194304 p
diem toverf
end
for i ulong n bound 4194304
put ob add p i get inp add o i
end
put obn 0 add p n
end

note emb: append one byte to ob
fn emb c uchar to void
p = get obn 0
if ge p 4194304
diem toverf
end
put ob p c
put obn 0 add p 1
end

note emu: append v in decimal to ob
fn emu v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
put d 0 uchar add rem x 10 48
k = ulong 1
x = div x 10
while gt x 0 bound 20
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
end
while gt k 0 bound 20
k = sub k 1
emb get d k
end
end

note eqx: do the n bytes of inp at o equal the text t
fn eqx o ulong n ulong t view uchar * to bool
if ne n len t
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 4194304
if ne get inp add o i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note eqs: do the n bytes of inp at a equal the n bytes at b (n at most 64)
fn eqs a ulong b ulong n ulong to bool
for i ulong n bound 64
if ne get inp add a i get inp add b i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

fn ishex c uchar to bool
ret or and ge c 48 le c 57 and ge c 97 le c 102
end

note vhex: is inp[o, o+n) exactly w lowercase hex digits (w at most 64)
fn vhex o ulong n ulong w ulong to bool
if ne n w
ret false
end
for i ulong w bound 64
if not ishex get inp add o i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note hx: FNV-1a 64 of the n bytes of inp at o (n at most 64), continuing from h
fn hx o ulong n ulong h ulong to ulong
x = h
for i ulong n bound 64
x = mul xor x ulong get inp add o i 1099511628211
end
ret x
end

note hash40: the hash of the 40 bytes of inp at k, high half folded into the low
fn hash40 k ulong to ulong
x = hx k 40 14695981039346656037
ret xor x shr x 32
end

note pslot: the slot of hp that holds the patch id at k, or the empty slot where it goes.
note At most 4096 of the 8192 slots are full, so an empty one comes within 4097 probes.
fn pslot k ulong to ulong
s = and hash40 k 8191
while true bound 8192
j = get hp s
if eq j 0
ret s
end
if eqs get so sub j 1 k 40
ret s
end
s = and add s 1 8191
end
ret s
end

note tslot: the slot of ht that holds the tree at k, or the empty slot where it goes
fn tslot k ulong to ulong
s = and hash40 k 8191
while true bound 8192
j = get ht s
if eq j 0
ret s
end
if eqs add get so sub j 1 82 k 40
ret s
end
s = and add s 1 8191
end
ret s
end

note rslot: the slot of hr that holds the receipt for the tree at t and the gate at g, or the
note empty slot where it goes. At most 16384 of the 32768 slots are full.
fn rslot t ulong g ulong to ulong
x = hx g 40 hx t 40 14695981039346656037
s = and xor x shr x 32 32767
while true bound 32768
j = get hr s
if eq j 0
ret s
end
o = get ro sub j 1
if eqs o t 40
if eqs add o 41 g 40
ret s
end
end
s = and add s 1 32767
end
ret s
end

note lend: the newline that ends line ln, which starts at p (e is the end of the file); refuse a
note blank line, a CR and a last line without its newline
fn lend p ulong e ulong ln ulong to ulong
q = p
note every pass looks at one byte of the file
while lt q e bound 4194305
c = get inp q
if eq c 10
if eq q p
diel tblank ln 0
end
ret q
end
if eq c 13
diel tcr ln 0
end
q = add q 1
end
diel tnonl ln 0
ret e
end

note split4: store the 4 TAB-separated fields of line ln, [p, q), in fld; refuse another count
fn split4 p ulong q ulong ln ulong to void
k = ulong 0
s = p
t = p
while lt t q bound 4194305
if eq get inp t 9
if ge k 3
diel tcols ln 0
end
put fld mul k 2 s
put fld add mul k 2 1 sub t s
k = add k 1
s = add t 1
end
t = add t 1
end
if ne k 3
diel tcols ln 0
end
put fld 6 s
put fld 7 sub q s
end

note fo / fl: offset and length of field k of the current line
fn fo k ulong to ulong
ret get fld mul k 2
end

fn fl k ulong to ulong
ret get fld add mul k 2 1
end

note srow: check STATE row r, the line [p, q); record its offset and rel; refuse a repeated
note patch. With every field checked, patch is at p, head at p+41, tree at p+82.
fn srow r ulong p ulong q ulong to void
ln = add r 2
split4 p q ln
chk vhex fo 0 fl 0 40 tbpa ln
chk vhex fo 1 fl 1 40 tbhd ln
chk vhex fo 2 fl 2 40 tbtr ln
o = fo 3
n = fl 3
x = ulong 0
if eqx o n rff
x = ulong 1
end
if eqx o n rdiv
x = ulong 2
end
if eqx o n rin
x = ulong 3
end
chk ne x 0 tbrel ln
put so r p
put sr r x
s = pslot p
j = get hp s
if ne j 0
diel tdupp ln add j 1
end
put hp s add r 1
end

note rrow: check RECEIPTS row i, the line [p, q); record its offset and verdict; refuse a
note repeated (tree, gate). With every field checked, tree is at p, gate at p+41.
fn rrow i ulong p ulong q ulong to void
ln = add i 2
split4 p q ln
chk vhex fo 0 fl 0 40 tbtr ln
chk vhex fo 1 fl 1 40 tbgt ln
o = fo 2
n = fl 2
x = ulong 0
if eqx o n vpass
x = ulong 1
end
if eqx o n vfail
x = ulong 2
end
chk ne x 0 tbvd ln
chk vhex fo 3 fl 3 64 tblog ln
put ro i p
put rv i x
s = rslot p add p 41
j = get hr s
if ne j 0
diel tdupr ln add j 1
end
put hr s add i 1
end

note pstate: check the STATE bytes [0, e): the header, then every row
fn pstate e ulong to void
if eq e 0
diel tempty 1 0
end
q = lend 0 e 1
if not eqx 0 q tshdr
diel tbsh 1 0
end
p = add q 1
r = ulong 0
note every pass consumes at least one byte of the file
while lt p e bound 4194305
if ge r 4096
diel tmanys add r 2 0
end
q = lend p e add r 2
srow r p q
r = add r 1
p = add q 1
end
put ns 0 r
end

note prec: check the RECEIPTS bytes [RB, e): the header, then every row
fn prec e ulong to void
if eq e RB
diel tempty 1 0
end
q = lend RB e 1
if not eqx RB sub q RB trhdr
diel tbrh 1 0
end
p = add q 1
i = ulong 0
note every pass consumes at least one byte of the file
while lt p e bound 4194305
if ge i 16384
diel tmanyr add i 2 0
end
q = lend p e add i 2
rrow i p q
i = add i 1
p = add q 1
end
end

note argx: copy argument ai, which must be exactly 40 lowercase hex digits, into inp at o;
note refuse with m
fn argx ai ulong o ulong m view uchar * to void
n = argread ai pb 0 4096
if ne n 40
diem m
end
for i ulong 40
c = get pb i
if not ishex c
diem m
end
put inp add o i c
end
end

note act: the decision for STATE row r, 0 merged, 1 merge, 2 queued, 3 rebase, 4 fail, 5 gate,
note 6 same; mg: an earlier row got merge; sn: an earlier row has the same tree
fn act r ulong mg bool sn bool to ulong
x = get sr r
if eq x 3
ret 0
end
j = get hr rslot add get so r 82 GO
if eq j 0
if sn
ret 6
end
ret 5
end
if eq get rv sub j 1 2
ret 4
end
if eq x 2
ret 3
end
if mg
ret 2
end
ret 1
end

note decide: decide every STATE row in input order, recording each tree as it is seen
fn decide to void
n = get ns 0
mg = false
for r ulong n bound 4096
s = tslot add get so r 82
sn = ne get ht s 0
if not sn
put ht s add r 1
end
a = act r mg sn
put sa r a
put cnt a add get cnt a 1
if eq a 1
mg = true
end
end
end

note emname: append the name of decision a
fn emname a ulong to void
if eq a 0
em n0
end
if eq a 1
em n1
end
if eq a 2
em n2
end
if eq a 3
em n3
end
if eq a 4
em vfail
end
if eq a 5
em n5
end
if eq a 6
em n6
end
end

note emq: append 'PATCH' 'HEAD' 'TREE' and a newline for the row whose line starts at p
fn emq p ulong to void
emi p 40
em q2
emi add p 41 40
em q2
emi add p 82 40
em q3
end

note emrow: append row r's plan line, and its call for merge and gate
fn emrow r ulong to void
p = get so r
a = get sa r
em pln
emname a
em sp
emi p 40
em sp
emi add p 41 40
em sp
emi add p 82 40
em tnl
if eq a 1
em fm
emq p
end
if eq a 5
em fg
emq p
end
end

fn main to int
if ne argcnt 6
w = write 2 tusage 0 len tusage
ret 2
end
argx 1 BO tbr
argx 2 GO tgt
e = load 3 0
pstate e
e = load 4 RB
prec e
decide
em h0
em h1
em pbr
emi BO 40
em pgt
emi GO 40
em pc0
emu get ns 0
em pc1
emu get cnt 0
em pc2
emu get cnt 1
em pc3
emu get cnt 2
em pc4
emu get cnt 3
em pc5
emu get cnt 4
em pc6
emu get cnt 5
em pc7
emu get cnt 6
em pv1
